            "definition": "Mingli Yuan proposes arithmetic universality: finite arithmetic syntax and finite witnessed computation may provide a common constructive presentation for task-relative languages, with additive-zero and multiplicative-unit boundary questions supplied by the opposite hypothesis named hypothesized-arithmetic-truth. The class of languages, translation, preservation relation, and universal property remain to be specified and proved."
